---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import LeadForm from '../../components/LeadForm.astro';
import ServiceCard from '../../components/ServiceCard.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Concrete Driveways Murrieta, CA | Installation & Replacement | Free Estimates"
  description="Professional concrete driveway installation and replacement in Murrieta, CA. Licensed contractors, quality materials, 10-year guarantee. Free estimates."
>
  <Hero
    headline="Concrete Driveways in Murrieta, CA"
    subheadline="New driveway installation or full replacement — built to last in Murrieta's inland climate with proper reinforcement and grading."
    ctaText="Get a Free Estimate"
  />

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:text-primary">
      <h2>Why Choose Concrete for Your Murrieta Driveway?</h2>
      <p>
        Concrete driveways outlast asphalt by decades in Murrieta's climate — typically 30–50 years
        with proper installation vs. 15–25 years for asphalt. Concrete doesn't soften in summer
        heat the way asphalt does, and it doesn't require sealing every few years.
        The initial cost is higher, but the lifetime value is significantly better.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Driveway Installation Process</h2>
      <p>
        We start by excavating existing pavement and grading the subbase to ensure proper drainage
        away from your home. We install a gravel base layer, then steel rebar or wire mesh
        reinforcement before pouring. Expansion joints are placed at precise intervals to control
        cracking. After pouring, the concrete is finished, cured, and sealed for maximum durability.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your project involves removing a tree or large roots near the driveway, we coordinate
        with <a href="https://murrietatreeexperts.com">tree service professionals</a> to handle
        root removal properly before we pour — roots under concrete will cause cracking and heaving
        as they grow.
      </p>

      <h2>Tree Roots and Driveways: A Critical Consideration</h2>
      <p>
        This is one of the most common issues we see in Murrieta — tree roots from established
        eucalyptus, oak, or ficus trees that have grown under older driveways, causing cracking
        and lifting. Before replacing a damaged driveway, a
        <a href="https://murrietatreeexperts.com/services/tree-removal">certified arborist</a>
        should assess whether root pruning or tree removal is necessary to prevent the same
        problem from recurring in 5–10 years.
      </p>

      <h2>After Your New Driveway</h2>
      <p>
        A new concrete driveway dramatically improves curb appeal. Many homeowners also
        refresh the surrounding
        <a href="https://landscapingmurrieta.com/services/landscape-design">landscaping</a>
        at the same time — new plants, mulch, and border edging that frames the new driveway beautifully.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary mb-6">More Concrete Services</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        {SITE_CONFIG.services.filter(s => s.href !== '/services/concrete-driveways').map((s) => (
          <ServiceCard title={s.title} description={s.description} href={s.href} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <LeadForm heading="Get Your Free Driveway Estimate" />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
